        Note above that the line containing only "ENDANSI" signifies
the end of the "regular" ansi screen and is followed by the 
activity indicators. 2 blank lines immediately below the ENDANSI are used
to clear indicators between tests of main and imbedded archives. (In the
case of this ansi, none is required since all ouput is in the same space).
Each of the following lines is self explanitory.
   Each of those lines starts with an ansi position command followed by 
the indicators themselves. Note that the last line contains trailing spaces 
to clear text left by the previous indicator. And that text may be appended
to the end of the file with no adverse affect (as is the case with this 
explanitory text).
   The only real advice that I can offer is keep trying until you get it 
right. That is the reason why THDDEMO.COM was altered. Good luck and 
REMEMBER... NO LINE CAN BE LONGER THAN 70 CHARACTERS!!!!
